race condition - is the concept where two  threads try to implement the thing at the same time 
example is like we trying to withdraw the money in bank symoltatiously and system do not know what to do with this 
operations 

or in the program level this happense a lot 

like we trying to mute the object with two thread 
int i = 0;
two threads try mute the i but this cause the race condititon where only single thread made real change 

we can actually correct it using the synchronized keyword that shut down one thread until another thread is not implemented

example in code :

class Counter
{
  int count;
  public synchronized void increment() // here we used this keyword 
  {
    count++;
  }
}

class Main
{
    public static void main(String a[]) throws InterruptedException
    {

      Counter cnt = new Counter();
 
        Runnable obj1 =  () -> 
            {
                for (int i = 0;i<1000;i++)
                {
                    cnt.increment();
                }
            };

        Runnable obj2 = () -> 
            {
                for (int i = 0;i<1000;i++)
                {
                    cnt.increment();
                }
            };


        
        Thread t1 = new Thread(obj1);
        Thread t2 = new Thread(obj2);

        

        t1.start();
        t2.start();

        t1.join();
        t2.join();

        System.out.println(cnt.count); // output alwayse will be the same 1000 + 1000
    }
}

